&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;The Virtual Private Cloud team develops the core networking layer of Nebius AI Cloud.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;We provide secure and isolated private networks, connectivity from cloud resources to internet and external networks, and networking services such as routing, security groups, load balancing and VPN connectivity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a Senior Technical Program Manager to drive complex initiatives spanning VPC, adjacent cloud services, and infrastructure layers. These may include launching VPC in new regions, supporting new hardware generations, improving platform scalability and resilience, evolving service architecture, and delivering new customer-facing networking capabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will work closely with developers, engineering managers, technical leads and product managers of VPC and adjacent teams. You will turn broad product and technical objectives into executable programs, define outcomes and acceptance criteria, expose dependencies and trade-offs, facilitate timely decisions, and coordinate delivery through validation, rollout, and operational readiness.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in technical program management, technical project management, engineering management, or a senior technical role involving the delivery of complex cross-team initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical background: you should be able to participate meaningfully in discussions about cloud networking and distributed systems, understand system boundaries and failure modes, and challenge assumptions without needing to be the primary architect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical knowledge of networking fundamentals such as IPv4 and IPv6 addressing, routing, network isolation, NAT, firewalls and load balancing. You should be comfortable learning and reasoning about the architecture of a production cloud-networking platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex technical topics clearly, facilitate decisions, and produce concise, actionable documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience coordinating initiatives involving multiple engineering teams with different priorities and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous problems, identify critical paths, manage risks, and adapt plans as requirements change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A practical, outcome-oriented approach and the ability to drive progress without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;It will be an added bonus if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating public-cloud or other large-scale infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with VPCs, SDN, network virtualization, or Linux networking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading programs focused on reliability, scalability, or operational improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing lightweight planning, risk-management, or operational-readiness processes for engineering organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
